[2026-03-14T22:00:15.448Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UFscE12onVg7LEgofmhPYT","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a comprehensive view of the application. Let me compile a thorough summary of my exploration findings.\n\n## LinearClone App Exploration - Complete Summary\n\nI've thoroughly explored the linear-clone application. Here are my findings:\n\n### 1. APP DIRECTORY STRUCTURE\n\n**Key directories:**\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/` - React source code\n  - `pages/` - Page components (IssueDetail.tsx, TeamIssues.tsx, etc.)\n  - `components/` - Reusable UI components\n  - `slices/` - Redux store slices\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/` - Backend API endpoints\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/tests/` - Playwright test specs\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/docs/` - Documentation (tests.md)\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/scripts/` - Database schema and seed scripts\n\n### 2. TEST SPECIFICATION (`/repo/apps/LinearClone/docs/tests.md`)\n\n**Sub-issues section tests (lines 1026-1055):**\n- Display sub-issues below description with \"Sub-issues\" heading and \"Add sub-issue\" button\n- Show \"No sub-issues\" message when empty\n- Display each sub-issue with identifier (e.g., \"ENG-11\"), title (clickable), status icon with color, priority icon\n- Click sub-issue title navigates to `/issue/{id}`\n- \"Add sub-issue\" button opens create issue modal with parent preset\n- Newly created sub-issue appears in list with todo status\n- Status change updates icon in parent's list\n- Multiple sub-issues display in consistent order\n\n**Activity section tests (lines 1066-1100):**\n- Display activity chronologically with actor avatar, name, action description, relative timestamp\n- Show three example entries: status change, assignee change, priority change\n- Entries ordered oldest first (top) to newest (bottom)\n- New activity entry appears at bottom when issue is updated\n- Shows \"Activity\" tab visual highlight\n\n**Comments section tests (lines 1068-1105):**\n- Display comments with author avatar, name, relative timestamp (e.g., \"2h ago\"), comment content\n- Comments ordered oldest first\n- Comment input box visible in comments view\n- New comment appears at bottom, input clears after submission\n- Tab switching between Activity and Comments tabs works\n- Comment submission creates activity entry\n- Notifications sent for subscribers\n- Multiple comments persist in order\n- Enter (Cmd/Ctrl) + Enter submits comment\n\n### 3. EXISTING TEST PATTERNS\n\n**Files:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/tests/issue-detail-header.spec.ts` and `/repo/apps/LinearClone/tests/issue-detail-description.spec.ts`\n\n**Test pattern structure:**\n1. Helper functions for API login and data fetching:\n   - `loginViaApi(baseURL, email, password)` - returns {token, user}\n   - `getTeams(baseURL, token)` - fetches teams list\n   - `getTeamIssues(baseURL, token, teamId)` - fetches team issues\n   - `updateIssueField(baseURL, token, issueId, field, value)` - API update helper\n   - `loginAndNavigateToIssue(page, baseURL, issueNumber)` - complete login + navigation flow\n\n2. Test structure:\n   ```typescript\n   test('test description', async ({ page, baseURL }) => {\n     // Setup via helper\n     // Perform actions with page.getByTestId()\n     // Assert with expect()\n   });\n   ```\n\n3. Common assertions:\n   - `toBeVisible()`, `toBeFocused()`, `toHaveClass()`, `toHaveValue()`, `toContainText()`\n   - Uses `data-testid` attributes for element selection\n\n### 4. ISSUE DETAIL PAGE COMPONENT (`/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/pages/IssueDetail.tsx`)\n\n**Page structure:**\n```\nIssueDetail (page)\n├── IssueHeader (issue title, status inline selector)\n├── IssueDescription (markdown editor)\n├── SubIssues (sub-issues list with \"Add sub-issue\" button)\n├── ActivityComments (tabs for activity history and comments)\n└── IssueSidebar (assignee, priority, labels, project, cycle, due date)\n```\n\n**Redux state from issueDetailSlice:**\n- `issue` - Current Issue object\n- `subIssues` - Array of SubIssue[]\n- `activity` - Array of ActivityEntry[]\n- `comments` - Array of Comment[]\n- `members`, `projects`, `cycles`, `allLabels` - For dropdowns/selectors\n\n### 5. SUB-ISSUES COMPONENT (`/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/SubIssues.tsx`)\n\n- Props: `parentIssue: Issue`, `subIssues: SubIssue[]`\n- Displays \"Sub-issues\" heading with \"Add sub-issue\" button\n- Shows \"No sub-issues\" when empty\n- Each row shows: status icon, priority icon, identifier, clickable title\n- Click title navigates to `/issue/{subIssueId}`\n- Click \"Add sub-issue\" dispatches `openCreateIssueModal({ parentId, teamId })`\n- testId: `sub-issues`, `sub-issue-row-{id}`, `sub-issue-title-{id}`, etc.\n\n### 6. ACTIVITY/COMMENTS COMPONENT (`/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/ActivityComments.tsx`)\n\n**Tabs:** \"Activity\" and \"Comments\" (state: `activeTab`)\n\n**Activity list:**\n- Shows ActivityEntry[] with `id`, `action`, `createdAt`, `memberName`\n- Avatar with member initials, name, action text, relative time\n- Empty state: \"No activity yet\"\n- Ordered oldest first\n- testId: `activity-list`, `activity-entry-{id}`\n\n**Comments list:**\n- Shows Comment[] with `id`, `content`, `createdAt`, `memberName`\n- Avatar, author name, relative timestamp, content\n- Empty state: \"No comments yet\"\n- Ordered oldest first\n- testId: `comments-list`, `comment-entry-{id}`\n\n**Comment input:**\n- Textarea with placeholder \"Write a comment...\"\n- Submit button (disabled if empty or submitting)\n- Keyboard handler: Cmd/Ctrl + Enter submits\n- Dispatches `addComment({ issueId, content })` async action\n- testId: `comment-input`, `comment-submit-btn`\n\n**Helper functions:**\n- `formatRelativeTime(dateStr)` - Returns \"just now\", \"{n}m ago\", \"{n}h ago\", \"{n}d ago\", or formatted date\n- `getInitials(name)` - Returns 2-char initials\n\n### 7. ISSUE HEADER COMPONENT (`/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/IssueHeader.tsx`)\n\n- Displays identifier (e.g., \"ENG-1\") and title (clickable to edit)\n- Inline title editor with Enter to save, Escape to cancel, blur to save\n- Validation: non-empty title required\n- Status selector: dropdown with all 6 statuses (backlog, todo, in_progress, in_review, done, cancelled)\n- Status changes via `updateIssueField({ issueId, field: 'status', value })`\n- testId: `issue-header-title`, `issue-header-status-btn`, `issue-header-status-dropdown`, etc.\n\n### 8. ISSUE SIDEBAR COMPONENT (`/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/IssueSidebar.tsx`)\n\n- Displays and allows changes to: status, priority, assignee, labels, project, cycle, due date\n- Each field has dropdown selector\n- Assignee search filtering\n- Priority order: urgent, high, medium, low, none\n- Label toggle (multi-select checkboxes)\n- Project search filtering\n- Cycle selector\n- Due date: HTML date input or clear button\n- All changes via `updateIssueField()` with appropriate field names\n\n### 9. NETLIFY FUNCTIONS FOR ISSUES\n\n**`/api/issue-detail` (GET)** - `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/issue-detail.ts`\n- Fetches full issue detail with:\n  - Issue object (all fields including parent_id)\n  - Sub-issues list (WHERE parent_id = issueId, ORDER BY created_at)\n  - Activity entries (WHERE issue_id = issueId, ORDER BY created_at ASC)\n  - Comments (WHERE issue_id = issueId, ORDER BY created_at ASC)\n  - Team members for assignee dropdown\n  - Projects and cycles lists\n  - All labels\n- Returns: `{ issue, subIssues, activity, comments, members, projects, cycles, allLabels }`\n\n**`/api/add-comment` (POST)** - `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/add-comment.ts`\n- Body: `{ issueId: string, content: string }`\n- Inserts comment into DB, creates activity entry \"added a comment\"\n- Creates notification for issue assignee (if different from commenter)\n- Returns: `{ comment: { id, content, createdAt, memberId, memberName, memberEmail } }`\n\n**`/api/update-issue` (PUT)** - `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/update-issue.ts`\n- Body: `{ issueId, field, value, labelIds? }`\n- Supported fields: title, description, status, priority, assigneeId, projectId, cycleId, dueDate, labels\n- Creates activity entry with descriptive action text for each field type\n- Sends notifications for assignee changes\n- Returns: `{ issue: {...}, activity: ActivityEntry | null }`\n\n### 10. PLAYWRIGHT CONFIG (`/repo/apps/LinearClone/playwright.config.ts`)\n\n```typescript\n{\n  testDir: './tests',\n  timeout: 60000,\n  expect.timeout: 10000,\n  fullyParallel: true,\n  forbidOnly: true,\n  retries: 0,\n  reporter: [replayReporter, json, html],\n  use: {\n    baseURL: 'http://localhost:8888',\n    actionTimeout: 15000,\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### 11. DATABASE SCHEMA (`/repo/apps/LinearClone/scripts/schema.ts`)\n\n**Key tables:**\n- `issues` - `id, team_id, title, description, status, priority, number, due_date, assignee_id, project_id, cycle_id, parent_id, created_at, updated_at`\n- `comments` - `id, issue_id, member_id, content, created_at`\n- `activity` - `id, issue_id, member_id, action, field, new_value, created_at`\n- `members` - `id, name, email, password_hash, password_salt, role, created_at`\n- `teams` - `id, name, identifier, description`\n- `issue_labels` - Junction table (issue_id, label_id)\n- `sessions`, `team_members`, `labels`, `projects`, `cycles`, `notifications`, etc.\n\n**Indexes on:** team_id, assignee_id, project_id, cycle_id, parent_id, issue_id (for comments and activity)\n\n### 12. REDUX SLICES\n\n**`issueDetailSlice.ts`:**\n- State: issue, subIssues, activity, comments, members, projects, cycles, allLabels, loading, error\n- Async thunks: `fetchIssueDetail(issueId)`, `updateIssueField(payload)`, `addComment(payload)`\n- Reducer actions: `clearIssueDetail()`\n- `addComment` fulfilled adds comment to array\n- `updateIssueField` fulfilled updates issue and appends activity entry if returned\n\n**`issuesSlice.ts`:**\n- State: myIssues, loading, error\n- Issue interface: id, title, description, status, priority, identifier, number, dueDate, teamId, assigneeId, projectId, cycleId, parentId, labels\n- Types: Issue, IssueLabel, CreateIssuePayload\n\n### 13. KEY DATA TYPES\n\n**SubIssue:**\n```typescript\n{ id, title, status, priority, identifier }\n```\n\n**ActivityEntry:**\n```typescript\n{ id, action, createdAt, memberId, memberName, memberEmail }\n```\n\n**Comment:**\n```typescript\n{ id, content, createdAt, memberId, memberName, memberEmail }\n```\n\n**Activity action text examples:**\n- \"changed title from X to Y\"\n- \"updated the description\"\n- \"changed status from Todo to In Progress\"\n- \"changed priority from Medium to Urgent\"\n- \"assigned to Alice\" or \"changed assignee from X to Y\"\n- \"set project to Auth Rewrite\"\n- \"updated labels\"\n- \"added a comment\"\n\nAll paths are absolute:\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/pages/IssueDetail.tsx`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/SubIssues.tsx`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/ActivityComments.tsx`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/IssueHeader.tsx`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/IssueSidebar.tsx`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/slices/issueDetailSlice.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/issue-detail.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/add-comment.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/update-issue.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/tests/issue-detail-header.spec.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/tests/issue-detail-description.spec.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/docs/tests.md`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/playwright.config.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/scripts/schema.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/scripts/seed-db.ts`"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a146777d6a302cf88 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 79424\ntool_uses: 29\nduration_ms: 58046</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b3a342c-e5c0-4c3a-aec1-6eee419ae688","uuid":"4afee543-2f01-4c4b-a010-3a9f87d830ef","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the linear-clone app in /repo/apps/. I need to understand:\n1. The app directory structure (list key files)\n2. The test spec file (docs/tests.md or similar) - specifically sections about sub-issues, activity, and comments\n3. Existing test files to understand patterns\n4. The issue detail page component and related sub-issue/activity/comment components\n5. The Netlify functions for issues (especially sub-issues, activity, comments)\n6. The playwright config\n7. The database schema (seed file or schema)\n8. The Redux store slices related to issues, comments, activity\n\nBe thorough - read the test spec, existing tests, components, and API functions.","agentId":"a146777d6a302cf88","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a comprehensive view of the application. Let me compile a thorough summary of my exploration findings.\n\n## LinearClone App Exploration - Complete Summary\n\nI've thoroughly explored the linear-clone application. Here are my findings:\n\n### 1. APP DIRECTORY STRUCTURE\n\n**Key directories:**\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/` - React source code\n  - `pages/` - Page components (IssueDetail.tsx, TeamIssues.tsx, etc.)\n  - `components/` - Reusable UI components\n  - `slices/` - Redux store slices\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/` - Backend API endpoints\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/tests/` - Playwright test specs\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/docs/` - Documentation (tests.md)\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/scripts/` - Database schema and seed scripts\n\n### 2. TEST SPECIFICATION (`/repo/apps/LinearClone/docs/tests.md`)\n\n**Sub-issues section tests (lines 1026-1055):**\n- Display sub-issues below description with \"Sub-issues\" heading and \"Add sub-issue\" button\n- Show \"No sub-issues\" message when empty\n- Display each sub-issue with identifier (e.g., \"ENG-11\"), title (clickable), status icon with color, priority icon\n- Click sub-issue title navigates to `/issue/{id}`\n- \"Add sub-issue\" button opens create issue modal with parent preset\n- Newly created sub-issue appears in list with todo status\n- Status change updates icon in parent's list\n- Multiple sub-issues display in consistent order\n\n**Activity section tests (lines 1066-1100):**\n- Display activity chronologically with actor avatar, name, action description, relative timestamp\n- Show three example entries: status change, assignee change, priority change\n- Entries ordered oldest first (top) to newest (bottom)\n- New activity entry appears at bottom when issue is updated\n- Shows \"Activity\" tab visual highlight\n\n**Comments section tests (lines 1068-1105):**\n- Display comments with author avatar, name, relative timestamp (e.g., \"2h ago\"), comment content\n- Comments ordered oldest first\n- Comment input box visible in comments view\n- New comment appears at bottom, input clears after submission\n- Tab switching between Activity and Comments tabs works\n- Comment submission creates activity entry\n- Notifications sent for subscribers\n- Multiple comments persist in order\n- Enter (Cmd/Ctrl) + Enter submits comment\n\n### 3. EXISTING TEST PATTERNS\n\n**Files:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/tests/issue-detail-header.spec.ts` and `/repo/apps/LinearClone/tests/issue-detail-description.spec.ts`\n\n**Test pattern structure:**\n1. Helper functions for API login and data fetching:\n   - `loginViaApi(baseURL, email, password)` - returns {token, user}\n   - `getTeams(baseURL, token)` - fetches teams list\n   - `getTeamIssues(baseURL, token, teamId)` - fetches team issues\n   - `updateIssueField(baseURL, token, issueId, field, value)` - API update helper\n   - `loginAndNavigateToIssue(page, baseURL, issueNumber)` - complete login + navigation flow\n\n2. Test structure:\n   ```typescript\n   test('test description', async ({ page, baseURL }) => {\n     // Setup via helper\n     // Perform actions with page.getByTestId()\n     // Assert with expect()\n   });\n   ```\n\n3. Common assertions:\n   - `toBeVisible()`, `toBeFocused()`, `toHaveClass()`, `toHaveValue()`, `toContainText()`\n   - Uses `data-testid` attributes for element selection\n\n### 4. ISSUE DETAIL PAGE COMPONENT (`/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/pages/IssueDetail.tsx`)\n\n**Page structure:**\n```\nIssueDetail (page)\n├── IssueHeader (issue title, status inline selector)\n├── IssueDescription (markdown editor)\n├── SubIssues (sub-issues list with \"Add sub-issue\" button)\n├── ActivityComments (tabs for activity history and comments)\n└── IssueSidebar (assignee, priority, labels, project, cycle, due date)\n```\n\n**Redux state from issueDetailSlice:**\n- `issue` - Current Issue object\n- `subIssues` - Array of SubIssue[]\n- `activity` - Array of ActivityEntry[]\n- `comments` - Array of Comment[]\n- `members`, `projects`, `cycles`, `allLabels` - For dropdowns/selectors\n\n### 5. SUB-ISSUES COMPONENT (`/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/SubIssues.tsx`)\n\n- Props: `parentIssue: Issue`, `subIssues: SubIssue[]`\n- Displays \"Sub-issues\" heading with \"Add sub-issue\" button\n- Shows \"No sub-issues\" when empty\n- Each row shows: status icon, priority icon, identifier, clickable title\n- Click title navigates to `/issue/{subIssueId}`\n- Click \"Add sub-issue\" dispatches `openCreateIssueModal({ parentId, teamId })`\n- testId: `sub-issues`, `sub-issue-row-{id}`, `sub-issue-title-{id}`, etc.\n\n### 6. ACTIVITY/COMMENTS COMPONENT (`/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/ActivityComments.tsx`)\n\n**Tabs:** \"Activity\" and \"Comments\" (state: `activeTab`)\n\n**Activity list:**\n- Shows ActivityEntry[] with `id`, `action`, `createdAt`, `memberName`\n- Avatar with member initials, name, action text, relative time\n- Empty state: \"No activity yet\"\n- Ordered oldest first\n- testId: `activity-list`, `activity-entry-{id}`\n\n**Comments list:**\n- Shows Comment[] with `id`, `content`, `createdAt`, `memberName`\n- Avatar, author name, relative timestamp, content\n- Empty state: \"No comments yet\"\n- Ordered oldest first\n- testId: `comments-list`, `comment-entry-{id}`\n\n**Comment input:**\n- Textarea with placeholder \"Write a comment...\"\n- Submit button (disabled if empty or submitting)\n- Keyboard handler: Cmd/Ctrl + Enter submits\n- Dispatches `addComment({ issueId, content })` async action\n- testId: `comment-input`, `comment-submit-btn`\n\n**Helper functions:**\n- `formatRelativeTime(dateStr)` - Returns \"just now\", \"{n}m ago\", \"{n}h ago\", \"{n}d ago\", or formatted date\n- `getInitials(name)` - Returns 2-char initials\n\n### 7. ISSUE HEADER COMPONENT (`/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/IssueHeader.tsx`)\n\n- Displays identifier (e.g., \"ENG-1\") and title (clickable to edit)\n- Inline title editor with Enter to save, Escape to cancel, blur to save\n- Validation: non-empty title required\n- Status selector: dropdown with all 6 statuses (backlog, todo, in_progress, in_review, done, cancelled)\n- Status changes via `updateIssueField({ issueId, field: 'status', value })`\n- testId: `issue-header-title`, `issue-header-status-btn`, `issue-header-status-dropdown`, etc.\n\n### 8. ISSUE SIDEBAR COMPONENT (`/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/IssueSidebar.tsx`)\n\n- Displays and allows changes to: status, priority, assignee, labels, project, cycle, due date\n- Each field has dropdown selector\n- Assignee search filtering\n- Priority order: urgent, high, medium, low, none\n- Label toggle (multi-select checkboxes)\n- Project search filtering\n- Cycle selector\n- Due date: HTML date input or clear button\n- All changes via `updateIssueField()` with appropriate field names\n\n### 9. NETLIFY FUNCTIONS FOR ISSUES\n\n**`/api/issue-detail` (GET)** - `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/issue-detail.ts`\n- Fetches full issue detail with:\n  - Issue object (all fields including parent_id)\n  - Sub-issues list (WHERE parent_id = issueId, ORDER BY created_at)\n  - Activity entries (WHERE issue_id = issueId, ORDER BY created_at ASC)\n  - Comments (WHERE issue_id = issueId, ORDER BY created_at ASC)\n  - Team members for assignee dropdown\n  - Projects and cycles lists\n  - All labels\n- Returns: `{ issue, subIssues, activity, comments, members, projects, cycles, allLabels }`\n\n**`/api/add-comment` (POST)** - `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/add-comment.ts`\n- Body: `{ issueId: string, content: string }`\n- Inserts comment into DB, creates activity entry \"added a comment\"\n- Creates notification for issue assignee (if different from commenter)\n- Returns: `{ comment: { id, content, createdAt, memberId, memberName, memberEmail } }`\n\n**`/api/update-issue` (PUT)** - `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/update-issue.ts`\n- Body: `{ issueId, field, value, labelIds? }`\n- Supported fields: title, description, status, priority, assigneeId, projectId, cycleId, dueDate, labels\n- Creates activity entry with descriptive action text for each field type\n- Sends notifications for assignee changes\n- Returns: `{ issue: {...}, activity: ActivityEntry | null }`\n\n### 10. PLAYWRIGHT CONFIG (`/repo/apps/LinearClone/playwright.config.ts`)\n\n```typescript\n{\n  testDir: './tests',\n  timeout: 60000,\n  expect.timeout: 10000,\n  fullyParallel: true,\n  forbidOnly: true,\n  retries: 0,\n  reporter: [replayReporter, json, html],\n  use: {\n    baseURL: 'http://localhost:8888',\n    actionTimeout: 15000,\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### 11. DATABASE SCHEMA (`/repo/apps/LinearClone/scripts/schema.ts`)\n\n**Key tables:**\n- `issues` - `id, team_id, title, description, status, priority, number, due_date, assignee_id, project_id, cycle_id, parent_id, created_at, updated_at`\n- `comments` - `id, issue_id, member_id, content, created_at`\n- `activity` - `id, issue_id, member_id, action, field, new_value, created_at`\n- `members` - `id, name, email, password_hash, password_salt, role, created_at`\n- `teams` - `id, name, identifier, description`\n- `issue_labels` - Junction table (issue_id, label_id)\n- `sessions`, `team_members`, `labels`, `projects`, `cycles`, `notifications`, etc.\n\n**Indexes on:** team_id, assignee_id, project_id, cycle_id, parent_id, issue_id (for comments and activity)\n\n### 12. REDUX SLICES\n\n**`issueDetailSlice.ts`:**\n- State: issue, subIssues, activity, comments, members, projects, cycles, allLabels, loading, error\n- Async thunks: `fetchIssueDetail(issueId)`, `updateIssueField(payload)`, `addComment(payload)`\n- Reducer actions: `clearIssueDetail()`\n- `addComment` fulfilled adds comment to array\n- `updateIssueField` fulfilled updates issue and appends activity entry if returned\n\n**`issuesSlice.ts`:**\n- State: myIssues, loading, error\n- Issue interface: id, title, description, status, priority, identifier, number, dueDate, teamId, assigneeId, projectId, cycleId, parentId, labels\n- Types: Issue, IssueLabel, CreateIssuePayload\n\n### 13. KEY DATA TYPES\n\n**SubIssue:**\n```typescript\n{ id, title, status, priority, identifier }\n```\n\n**ActivityEntry:**\n```typescript\n{ id, action, createdAt, memberId, memberName, memberEmail }\n```\n\n**Comment:**\n```typescript\n{ id, content, createdAt, memberId, memberName, memberEmail }\n```\n\n**Activity action text examples:**\n- \"changed title from X to Y\"\n- \"updated the description\"\n- \"changed status from Todo to In Progress\"\n- \"changed priority from Medium to Urgent\"\n- \"assigned to Alice\" or \"changed assignee from X to Y\"\n- \"set project to Auth Rewrite\"\n- \"updated labels\"\n- \"added a comment\"\n\nAll paths are absolute:\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/pages/IssueDetail.tsx`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/SubIssues.tsx`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/ActivityComments.tsx`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/IssueHeader.tsx`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/IssueSidebar.tsx`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/slices/issueDetailSlice.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/issue-detail.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/add-comment.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/update-issue.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/tests/issue-detail-header.spec.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/tests/issue-detail-description.spec.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/docs/tests.md`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/playwright.config.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/scripts/schema.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/scripts/seed-db.ts`"}],"totalDurationMs":58046,"totalTokens":79424,"totalToolUseCount":29,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4422,"cache_read_input_tokens":71534,"output_tokens":3467,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4422},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
